; /XTRA
;; band-split.ab3 -- the back playfield's two bands at their own speeds, for a few copper
;; moves instead of DisplayScroll's whole list.
;; Compile in UAE. Not part of the game. Fourth proof of the scrolling options in
;; the main project's AMIGA_RENDERER note ("Parallax and scrolling options").
;;
;; line-scroll.ab3 proved the picture (2026-10-14) but DisplayScroll cost 52 lines a
;; frame: it rewrites BPLCON1 and both modulos on all 207 lines every frame. Only the
;; boundary between the clouds and the hills needs anything, so here two CustomStrings
;; sit at the boundary (in rows that are sky in the back bitmap, so a line half way
;; through the change shows nothing):
;;   at list line #BAND_LINE - 2: the pointers of back planes 0 and 1 (BPL2PT, BPL4PT)
;;   at list line #BAND_LINE - 1: back planes 2 and 3 (BPL6PT, BPL8PT) and BPLCON1
;; Split over two lines so each group of moves fits in the horizontal blank. The values
;; are worked out the way displaylib.ab3 does it for a dual playfield (_displaydbmap2 and
;; its bp1 table): x in quarter pixels; the low 8 bits (64 px at fetch mode 3) are the
;; fine delay, 255 less them, packed into BPLCON1; the rest, as bytes (8 per 64 px), is
;; added to the plane pointer of the bitmap row. The front's part of BPLCON1 is the same
;; one the list's header already has, so the front does not move.
;;
;; The camera now moves rightwards for ever, so nothing reverses. The front is a 128 px
;; pattern and wraps at 512; the clouds (a quarter of the camera) and the hills (half)
;; wrap at 768. Keys:
;;   1 to 5  camera speed 0.5, 1, 1.25, 2, 3 px a frame (the HUD shows 1 to 5 boxes)
;;   R       the back's bands at whole pixels or at the quarter pixel (a red box in the
;;           HUD means whole pixels)
;;   U       stop and restart the band updates (a dark red box in the HUD means stopped;
;;           the hills then keep the last position they were given)
;;   Esc     quit and write band-split-results.txt
;;
;; First run (2026-10-14): the bands worked, R made no visible difference and the
;; judder is the sub-pixel steps of a slow layer (smoother the faster it goes). But the
;; band update, two CustomStrings built from Mki$ every frame, took 44 lines: the cost was
;; the Blitz strings. So the strings are now built once, and each frame only the nine
;; value words are poked into the copper list, found through the CopList object
;; (Addr CopList, then its customs pointer). The poke is used only if both strings' first
;; register words are where that layout puts them; else it falls back to CustomString.
;; The results file says which ran. Also seen on the first run: after scrolling a
;; distance, the whole display dropped by 1 pixel.
;;
;; Second run (2026-10-14): the "drop" is a vertical seam in the FRONT playfield, about
;; 137 px in: right of it the pillars and ground are one line higher, as if that part of
;; each line came from the next bitmap row. The back is not split. It comes and goes as
;; the scroll moves, and it happens with the band updates stopped (U), so it is not the
;; band code. Suspect: fetch mode 3's fetch against the fine scroll. More keys to find it:
;;   S       stop and restart the camera; while stopped, the cursor keys left and right
;;           move it a quarter pixel a frame
;;   F       switch between fetch mode 3 (lists 0 and 1, the band split) and fetch mode
;;           1 (lists 2 and 3, no band split: the hills follow the clouds). A yellow box
;;           in the HUD means fetch mode 1.
;; The thin bar in the HUD, from x = #BAR_X, is the front's x within its 64 px fetch
;; block (0 to 63 px): the front's fine scroll.
;;
;; Then the user saw the seam scroll along with the picture and out of view: so it was in
;; the bitmap position, not the fetch. The cause was the front's wrap (QWrap wraps once;
;; see the main loop), not fetch mode 3. Fixed with a loop. S, the cursor keys and F stay
;; for checking.
;;
;; Third run: no seam at any speed. The poke path ran, but the update still took 25
;; lines (all nine words, function calls and divisions every frame). Now BPLCON1 comes
;; from tables and the pointers are poked only when the hills cross a 64 px block
;; (PokeBand{}).
;;
;; What to look at and report
;; 1. The bands exactly as on the third run: the hills smooth, with no jump each 64 px
;;    (where the pointers are now poked), and no seam.
;; 2. The results file: the band update's lines, average and worst.
;; The results file has the bob load (72 lines in dual-playfield.ab3) and the lines the
;; band update takes (44 by CustomString, 52 by DisplayScroll).

WBStartup

;; =======================================================
;; CONSTANTS
;; =======================================================

#RAW_KEY_1   = $01
#RAW_KEY_5   = $05
#RAW_KEY_R   = $13
#RAW_KEY_U     = $16
#RAW_KEY_S     = $21
#RAW_KEY_F     = $23
#RAW_KEY_ESC   = $45
#RAW_KEY_RIGHT = $4E
#RAW_KEY_LEFT  = $4F

;; The same display at fetch mode 1, on lists 2 and 3, for the seam hunt (F). No band
;; split there: its values would need fetch mode 1's sums.
#HUD_FLAGS_FM1   = $11014
#WORLD_FLAGS_FM1 = $11038

;; The fine-scroll bar in the HUD: the front's x within its 64 px fetch block, one pixel
;; of bar a pixel, from x = #BAR_X.
#BAR_X = 100

;; The CopList object (displaylib.ab3, NEWTYPE .mycop): the pointer to its custom copper
;; area is the eighth long. CustomString puts a string at customs + 4 * CCOffset: two
;; longs (a no-op move and the wait), then the moves, each a register word and a value
;; word. These are the byte offsets of the value words, from customs.
#MYCOP_CUSTOMS = 28
#POKE_FIRST    = 10
#POKE_SECOND   = 34

;; The hills' x in quarter pixels, less the fine part: changes once every 64 px.
#HILL_BLOCK_MASK = $FF00

#HUD_YPOS   = 44
#HUD_H      = 16
#LIST_GAP   = 3
#VIEW_H     = 208
#VIEW_TOP   = 32
#VIEW_W     = 320
#COPPER_COLORS = 32

;; 4 planes, smooth scroll, AGA colours, fetch mode 3; the world adds dual playfield and
;; counts 8 planes (two playfields of 4).
#HUD_FLAGS   = $13014
#WORLD_FLAGS = $13038

;; Two CustomStrings: each is 2 instructions (the wait) plus its moves. The first has 4
;; moves (6 in all) and starts at offset 0, the second 5 (7 in all) at offset 6.
#BAND_CUSTOMS  = 13
#STRING_B_SLOT = 6

;; BPLCON3 is the library default $c00 XOR this: PF2OF 16 rather than 8.
#PLAYFIELD2_OFFSET_16 = $1c00

#DISPLAY_ADJUST_START = -1
#DISPLAY_ADJUST_STOP  = -1

;; Bitmaps: 0 and 1 the front pair, 2 the back, 3 the HUD band, 4 the shape source.
#BM_A     = 0
#BM_B     = 1
#BM_BACK  = 2
#BM_HUD   = 3
#BM_SHAPE = 4
#FRONT_W  = 1024
#BACK_W   = 1152
#PERIOD   = 768
#FRONT_WRAP = 512
#WORLD_H  = 256
#HUD_W    = 384

;; The hills band starts at list line #BAND_LINE, bitmap row #VIEW_TOP + #BAND_LINE (112,
;; between the clouds at 40 to 79 and the hills at 140 to 207).
#BAND_LINE = 80

;; Copper registers: the even (back) planes' pointers, high word, and BPLCON1.
#BPL2PTH = $E4
#BPL4PTH = $EC
#BPL6PTH = $F4
#BPL8PTH = $FC
#BPLCON1 = $102

#BOB_SHAPE  = 0
#TILE       = 16
#BOB_BYTES  = 16384

#SPEEDS      = 5
#BOBS        = 8
#WORK_LINE   = 80
#LINES_PAL   = 312

;; =======================================================
;; GLOBALS
;; =======================================================

quitFlag.w = False
drawBm.w = #BM_B
drawBuf.w = 1
frameCount.l = 0
speedIndex.w = 2
wholePixels.w = False
rWasDown.w = False
cameraX.q = 0
frontX.q = 0
cloudX.q = 0
hillX.q = 0
viewX.w = 0
startLine.l = 0
endLine.l = 0
bobLines.l = 0
bobFrames.l = 0
bobSum.l = 0
bobMax.l = 0
bandLines.l = 0
bandSum.l = 0
bandMax.l = 0
backBytesPerRow.l = 0
copListAddress.l = 0
customsAddress.l = 0
pokeMode.w = False
bandFrozen.w = False
uWasDown.w = False
cameraStopped.w = False
sWasDown.w = False
fetchModeOne.w = False
fWasDown.w = False
worldList.w = 1
fineX.w = 0

Dim speedTable.q(#SPEEDS - 1)
speedTable(0) = 0.5
speedTable(1) = 1
speedTable(2) = 1.25
speedTable(3) = 2
speedTable(4) = 3

Dim backPlane.l(3)
Dim frontScrollPart.l(255)
Dim backScrollPart.l(255)
lastHillBlock.l = -1

;; =======================================================
;; ALLOC (AMIGA MODE)
;; =======================================================

BitMap #BM_A, #FRONT_W, #WORLD_H, 4
BitMap #BM_B, #FRONT_W, #WORLD_H, 4
BitMap #BM_BACK, #BACK_W, #WORLD_H, 4
BitMap #BM_HUD, #HUD_W, #HUD_H, 4
BitMap #BM_SHAPE, 16, #TILE, 4

;; The back's planes, from the Blitz BitMap object: bytes per row at 0, plane pointers
;; from 8 (the layout displaylib.ab3 reads).
backBytesPerRow = Peek.w(Addr BitMap(#BM_BACK))
For planeIndex.w = 0 To 3
  backPlane(planeIndex) = Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#BM_BACK) + 8 + planeIndex*4)
Next

;; 0 the sky; 1 to 7 reds; 8 to 15 yellows; 16 black; 17 to 23 blues; 24 to 31 greys.
InitPalette 0, #COPPER_COLORS
AGAPalRGB 0, 0, 92, 148, 252
For colourIndex.w = 1 To 7
  AGAPalRGB 0, colourIndex, 100 + colourIndex*22, 0, 0
  AGAPalRGB 0, colourIndex + 8, 100 + colourIndex*22, 100 + colourIndex*22, 0
  AGAPalRGB 0, colourIndex + 16, 0, 0, 100 + colourIndex*22
  AGAPalRGB 0, colourIndex + 24, 60 + colourIndex*25, 60 + colourIndex*25, 60 + colourIndex*25
Next
AGAPalRGB 0, 8, 255, 255, 0
AGAPalRGB 0, 16, 0, 0, 0
AGAPalRGB 0, 24, 40, 40, 40

;; =======================================================
;; DISPLAY (BLITZ MODE)
;; =======================================================

BLITZ

Buffer 0, #BOB_BYTES
Buffer 1, #BOB_BYTES

;; Beam line: VPOSR bit 0 is V8, VHPOSR high byte V0 to V7. Masked before dividing
;; because bit 31 is a flag and the long is negative.
Function.l RasterLine{}
  rawPosition.l = Peek.l($dff004)
  Function Return (rawPosition AND $1ff00)/256
End Function

;; A 16 bit value as the signed word Mki$ takes.
Function.l SignedWord{value.l}
  value = value AND $ffff
  If value > 32767 Then value = value - 65536
  Function Return value
End Function

;; One playfield's part of BPLCON1 for a delay of 0 to 255 quarter pixels, in the
;; playfield 1 bits: delay bits 0-1 at 8-9, bits 2-5 at 0-3, bits 6-7 at 10-11 (checked
;; against displaylib's bp1 table). Playfield 2's part is this times 16.
Function.l ScrollPart{delay.l}
  Function Return (delay AND 3)*256 + ((delay/4) AND 15) + ((delay/64) AND 3)*1024
End Function

;; The two copper strings at the boundary, from the front's and the hills' x.
Statement UpdateBand{}
  SHARED frontX, hillX, backPlane(), backBytesPerRow
  frontQuarter.l = Int(frontX*4)
  hillQuarter.l = Int(hillX*4)
  control.l = ScrollPart{255 - (frontQuarter AND 255)} + ScrollPart{255 - (hillQuarter AND 255)}*16
  coarseBytes.l = (hillQuarter/256)*8
  ;; Planes 0 and 1 are set at the end of line #BAND_LINE - 2, for the next line's row.
  rowStart.l = (#VIEW_TOP + #BAND_LINE - 1)*backBytesPerRow + coarseBytes
  pointer0.l = backPlane(0) + rowStart
  pointer1.l = backPlane(1) + rowStart
  firstString$ = Mki$(#BPL2PTH) + Mki$(SignedWord{pointer0/65536}) + Mki$(#BPL2PTH + 2) + Mki$(SignedWord{pointer0})
  firstString$ = firstString$ + Mki$(#BPL4PTH) + Mki$(SignedWord{pointer1/65536}) + Mki$(#BPL4PTH + 2) + Mki$(SignedWord{pointer1})
  ;; Planes 2 and 3 and BPLCON1 at the end of line #BAND_LINE - 1, one row further on.
  rowStart = rowStart + backBytesPerRow
  pointer2.l = backPlane(2) + rowStart
  pointer3.l = backPlane(3) + rowStart
  secondString$ = Mki$(#BPL6PTH) + Mki$(SignedWord{pointer2/65536}) + Mki$(#BPL6PTH + 2) + Mki$(SignedWord{pointer2})
  secondString$ = secondString$ + Mki$(#BPL8PTH) + Mki$(SignedWord{pointer3/65536}) + Mki$(#BPL8PTH + 2) + Mki$(SignedWord{pointer3})
  secondString$ = secondString$ + Mki$(#BPLCON1) + Mki$(SignedWord{control})
  CustomString 1, 0, #BAND_LINE - 2, firstString$
  CustomString 1, #STRING_B_SLOT, #BAND_LINE - 1, secondString$
End Statement

;; The band's eight pointer words, for the hills' x in quarter pixels. Above PokeBand{},
;; which calls it.
Statement PokeBandPointers{hillQuarter.l}
  SHARED backPlane(), backBytesPerRow, customsAddress
  rowStart.l = (#VIEW_TOP + #BAND_LINE - 1)*backBytesPerRow + (hillQuarter/256)*8
  pointer.l = backPlane(0) + rowStart
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_FIRST, SignedWord{pointer/65536}
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_FIRST + 4, SignedWord{pointer}
  pointer = backPlane(1) + rowStart
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_FIRST + 8, SignedWord{pointer/65536}
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_FIRST + 12, SignedWord{pointer}
  rowStart = rowStart + backBytesPerRow
  pointer = backPlane(2) + rowStart
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_SECOND, SignedWord{pointer/65536}
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_SECOND + 4, SignedWord{pointer}
  pointer = backPlane(3) + rowStart
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_SECOND + 8, SignedWord{pointer/65536}
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_SECOND + 12, SignedWord{pointer}
End Statement

;; The same values as UpdateBand{}, poked straight into the value words of the two strings
;; it left in the copper list. The third run did all nine words every frame, with
;; ScrollPart{} and SignedWord{} calls and divisions, and took 25 lines. Now BPLCON1 comes
;; from two tables built once (frontScrollPart() and backScrollPart(), indexed by the fine
;; position in quarter pixels), and the eight pointer words are poked only when the hills
;; cross into another 64 px block (#HILL_BLOCK_MASK), about one frame in 32 at 2 px a frame.
Statement PokeBand{}
  SHARED frontX, hillX, customsAddress, lastHillBlock, frontScrollPart(), backScrollPart()
  frontQuarter.l = Int(frontX*4)
  hillQuarter.l = Int(hillX*4)
  control.l = frontScrollPart(frontQuarter AND 255) + backScrollPart(hillQuarter AND 255)
  If control > 32767 Then control = control - 65536
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_SECOND + 16, control
  hillBlock.l = hillQuarter AND #HILL_BLOCK_MASK
  If hillBlock <> lastHillBlock
    lastHillBlock = hillBlock
    PokeBandPointers{hillQuarter}
  EndIf
End Statement

;; The two BPLCON1 tables, indexed by the fine position (0 to 255 quarter pixels): the
;; delay is 255 less it. The back's part is the front's in the playfield 2 bits (times 16).
Statement BuildScrollTables{}
  SHARED frontScrollPart(), backScrollPart()
  For fineIndex.w = 0 To 255
    frontScrollPart(fineIndex) = ScrollPart{255 - fineIndex}
    backScrollPart(fineIndex) = ScrollPart{255 - fineIndex}*16
  Next
End Statement

;; The speed as 1 to 5 white boxes, and a red box at the right for whole pixels.
Statement DrawHud{}
  SHARED speedIndex, wholePixels, bandFrozen, fetchModeOne
  Use BitMap #BM_HUD
  Cls 0
  For boxIndex.w = 0 To speedIndex
    Boxf 8 + boxIndex*12, 4, 15 + boxIndex*12, 11, 7
  Next
  If wholePixels = True Then Boxf 296, 4, 303, 11, 4
  If bandFrozen = True Then Boxf 284, 4, 291, 11, 2
  If fetchModeOne = True Then Boxf 272, 4, 279, 11, 9
End Statement

;; The front: ground in pens 1 and 2, a tall pillar in pen 3 every 128 px.
Statement DrawFront{bitmapIndex.w}
  Use BitMap bitmapIndex
  Cls 0
  For columnIndex.w = 0 To #FRONT_W/#TILE - 1
    pen.w = 1
    If columnIndex MOD 2 = 1 Then pen = 2
    Boxf columnIndex*#TILE, 208, columnIndex*#TILE + #TILE - 1, 239, pen
  Next
  For pillarX.w = 48 To #FRONT_W - 64 Step 128
    Boxf pillarX, 40, pillarX + 23, 207, 3
  Next
End Statement

;; One cloud and one hill per 192 px, four in the 768 px period, drawn again at x + 768
;; where it fits. A marker in each band at x = 0 and x = 768.
Statement DrawBackPiece{pieceX.w}
  Boxf pieceX + 16, 48, pieceX + 111, 79, 5
  Boxf pieceX + 32, 40, pieceX + 79, 47, 5
  Boxf pieceX + 120, 160, pieceX + 183, 207, 6
  Boxf pieceX + 136, 140, pieceX + 167, 159, 6
End Statement

Statement DrawBack{}
  Use BitMap #BM_BACK
  Cls 0
  For pieceX.w = 0 To #BACK_W - 192 Step 192
    DrawBackPiece{pieceX}
  Next
  Boxf 0, 36, 3, 95, 7
  Boxf #PERIOD, 36, #PERIOD + 3, 95, 7
  Boxf 0, 128, 3, 207, 7
  Boxf #PERIOD, 128, #PERIOD + 3, 207, 7
End Statement

Statement MakeShapes{}
  Use BitMap #BM_SHAPE
  Cls 0
  Circlef 7, 7, 7, 4
  Circlef 7, 7, 3, 7
  GetaShape #BOB_SHAPE, 0, 0, #TILE, #TILE
End Statement

BBlitMode CookieMode
MakeShapes{}
DrawFront{#BM_A}
DrawFront{#BM_B}
DrawBack{}
DrawHud{}

InitCopList 0, #HUD_YPOS, #HUD_H, #HUD_FLAGS, 0, #COPPER_COLORS, 0
InitCopList 1, #HUD_YPOS + #HUD_H + #LIST_GAP, #VIEW_H, #WORLD_FLAGS, 0, 0, #BAND_CUSTOMS
DisplayAdjust 0, 0, 0, 0, #DISPLAY_ADJUST_START, #DISPLAY_ADJUST_STOP
DisplayAdjust 1, 0, 0, 0, #DISPLAY_ADJUST_START, #DISPLAY_ADJUST_STOP
DisplayControls 1, 0, #PLAYFIELD2_OFFSET_16, 0
InitCopList 2, #HUD_YPOS, #HUD_H, #HUD_FLAGS_FM1, 0, #COPPER_COLORS, 0
InitCopList 3, #HUD_YPOS + #HUD_H + #LIST_GAP, #VIEW_H, #WORLD_FLAGS_FM1, 0, 0, 0
DisplayAdjust 2, 0, 0, 0, #DISPLAY_ADJUST_START, #DISPLAY_ADJUST_STOP
DisplayAdjust 3, 0, 0, 0, #DISPLAY_ADJUST_START, #DISPLAY_ADJUST_STOP
DisplayControls 3, 0, #PLAYFIELD2_OFFSET_16, 0
CreateDisplay 0, 1
DisplayPalette 0, 0
DisplayBitMap 0, #BM_HUD, 0, 0
DisplayBitMap 1, drawBm, 0, #VIEW_TOP, #BM_BACK, 0, #VIEW_TOP
BuildScrollTables{}
UpdateBand{}
;; Find the strings in the copper list, and poke them only if both register words are
;; where the layout says.
copListAddress = Addr CopList(1)
customsAddress = Peek.l(copListAddress + #MYCOP_CUSTOMS)
If customsAddress <> 0
  If Peek.w(customsAddress + #POKE_FIRST - 2) = #BPL2PTH
    If Peek.w(customsAddress + #POKE_SECOND - 2) = #BPL6PTH Then pokeMode = True
  EndIf
EndIf
BlitzKeys On

While quitFlag = False
  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_ESC) Then quitFlag = True
  For keyIndex.w = 0 To #SPEEDS - 1
    If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_1 + keyIndex)
      If speedIndex <> keyIndex
        speedIndex = keyIndex
        DrawHud{}
      EndIf
    EndIf
  Next
  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_R)
    If rWasDown = False
      wholePixels = NOT wholePixels
      DrawHud{}
    EndIf
    rWasDown = True
  Else
    rWasDown = False
  EndIf
  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_U)
    If uWasDown = False
      bandFrozen = NOT bandFrozen
      DrawHud{}
    EndIf
    uWasDown = True
  Else
    uWasDown = False
  EndIf

  ;; The camera only ever moves right. The front wraps on its 128 px pattern, the bands
  ;; on the 768 px period.
  ;; S stops the camera; while stopped the cursor keys move it a quarter pixel a frame.
  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_S)
    If sWasDown = False Then cameraStopped = NOT cameraStopped
    sWasDown = True
  Else
    sWasDown = False
  EndIf
  ;; F switches between the fetch mode 3 lists (0 and 1) and the fetch mode 1 lists (2 and 3).
  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_F)
    If fWasDown = False
      fetchModeOne = NOT fetchModeOne
      VWait
      If fetchModeOne = True
        worldList = 3
        CreateDisplay 2, 3
        DisplayPalette 2, 0
        DisplayBitMap 2, #BM_HUD, 0, 0
      Else
        worldList = 1
        CreateDisplay 0, 1
        DisplayPalette 0, 0
        DisplayBitMap 0, #BM_HUD, 0, 0
      EndIf
      DrawHud{}
    EndIf
    fWasDown = True
  Else
    fWasDown = False
  EndIf

  If cameraStopped = False
    cameraX = cameraX + speedTable(speedIndex)
  Else
    If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_RIGHT) Then cameraX = cameraX + 0.25
    If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_LEFT) Then cameraX = cameraX - 0.25
    If cameraX < 0 Then cameraX = cameraX + #PERIOD*4
  EndIf
  If cameraX >= #PERIOD*4 Then cameraX = cameraX - #PERIOD*4
  ;; Not QWrap: it wraps once, not to the remainder, so a camera of up to 3,072 left the
  ;; front at up to 2,560, past its 1,024 px bitmap, and the display read on into the next
  ;; row: the seam of the second run.
  frontX = cameraX
  While frontX >= #FRONT_WRAP
    frontX = frontX - #FRONT_WRAP
  Wend
  cloudX = cameraX/4
  While cloudX >= #PERIOD
    cloudX = cloudX - #PERIOD
  Wend
  hillX = cameraX/2
  While hillX >= #PERIOD
    hillX = hillX - #PERIOD
  Wend
  If wholePixels = True
    cloudX = Int(cloudX)
    hillX = Int(hillX)
  EndIf
  viewX = Int(frontX)

  ;; The same bob load as the earlier proofs.
  While RasterLine{} < #WORK_LINE
  Wend
  Use BitMap drawBm
  startLine = RasterLine{}
  UnBuffer drawBuf
  For bobIndex.w = 0 To #BOBS - 1
    BBlit drawBuf, #BOB_SHAPE, viewX + 20 + bobIndex*36, 112 + (bobIndex MOD 2)*48
  Next
  endLine = RasterLine{}
  bobLines = endLine - startLine
  If bobLines < 0 Then bobLines = bobLines + #LINES_PAL

  VWait
  DisplayBitMap worldList, drawBm, frontX, #VIEW_TOP, #BM_BACK, cloudX, #VIEW_TOP
  ;; The fine-scroll bar: the front's x within its 64 px fetch block.
  fineX = viewX AND 63
  Use BitMap #BM_HUD
  Boxf #BAR_X, 13, #BAR_X + 64, 14, 0
  Boxf #BAR_X, 13, #BAR_X + fineX, 14, 7
  startLine = RasterLine{}
  If bandFrozen = False AND worldList = 1
    If pokeMode = True
      PokeBand{}
    Else
      UpdateBand{}
    EndIf
  EndIf
  endLine = RasterLine{}
  bandLines = endLine - startLine
  If bandLines < 0 Then bandLines = bandLines + #LINES_PAL

  If frameCount >= 10
    bobFrames = bobFrames + 1
    bobSum = bobSum + bobLines
    If bobLines > bobMax Then bobMax = bobLines
    bandSum = bandSum + bandLines
    If bandLines > bandMax Then bandMax = bandLines
  EndIf

  If drawBm = #BM_A
    drawBm = #BM_B
    drawBuf = 1
  Else
    drawBm = #BM_A
    drawBuf = 0
  EndIf
  frameCount = frameCount + 1
Wend

AMIGA
If WriteFile(0, "sparky-dave:game/proofs/results/band-split-results.txt")
  FileOutput 0
  NPrint "band-split: HUD $", Hex$(#HUD_FLAGS), ", world $", Hex$(#WORLD_FLAGS), ", customs ", #BAND_CUSTOMS, ", ", frameCount, " frames"
  If bobFrames > 0
    NPrint "bob load (", #BOBS, " bobs from line ", #WORK_LINE, "): average lines ", bobSum/bobFrames, ", worst ", bobMax
    NPrint "band update each frame: average lines ", bandSum/bobFrames, ", worst ", bandMax
  EndIf
  If pokeMode = True
    NPrint "band update by poking the copper list (customs at $", Hex$(customsAddress), ")"
  Else
    NPrint "band update by CustomString: the poke check failed (CopList at $", Hex$(copListAddress), ", customs read as $", Hex$(customsAddress), ")"
  EndIf
  NPrint "back bitmap: ", backBytesPerRow, " bytes a row, plane 0 at $", Hex$(backPlane(0))
  NPrint ""
  NPrint "For comparison: dual-playfield.ab3 72 lines of bobs; line-scroll.ab3 75 lines of"
  NPrint "bobs and 52 lines of DisplayScroll a frame."
  CloseFile 0
EndIf
End
